{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "divergence_mpas_l2",
    "description": "Convergence driver for grids/mpas/rules/fv_divergence_cell on the icosahedral level-2 mesh (162 cells, 480 edges, 320 vertices; grids/mpas/mesh/level2.esm mounted as the `mesh` subsystem) \u2014 one member of the divergence_mpas refinement family (levels 0/1/2; tests/conformance/convergence/divergence_mpas). This realizes the rebinding recipe documented in problems/divergence_mpas.esm: subsystem ref paths cannot be metaparameterized (esm-spec 9.7.6 binds sizes, not file refs), so each refinement level is its own thin problem file binding the grid metaparameters at the import edge and mounting its mesh. Unlike the exactness driver's curl flux (which the TRiSK divergence annihilates to rounding), this flux has NONZERO analytic divergence, giving a measurable discretization error: psi = P2(z) = (3 z^2 - 1)/2 (the l=2 zonal harmonic, z = sin(lat)), V = grad_s psi = 3 z (e_z - z x), and div_s V = laplacian_s psi = -l(l+1) psi = -3 (3 z^2 - 1) exactly on the unit sphere. The per-edge normal flux is the midpoint sample F(e) = V(x_e) . n_e at the MPAS edge location x_e = normalize(x_c1 + x_c2), n_e = normalize(x_c2 - x_c1) (tangent at x_e since |x_c1| = |x_c2| = 1), [c1, c2] = cellsOnEdge(e); because n_e is perpendicular to x_e this collapses to F(e) = 3 z_e n_e,z. Both the flux const array and the analytic per-cell divergence d(i) = -3 (3 sin(latCell(i))^2 - 1) in the test reference were computed at fixture-authoring time from EXACTLY these formulas over the mesh file's published latCell/lonCell/cellsOnEdge arrays (the same authoring discipline as the mesh data itself; byte-reproducible from the serialized mesh). Dynamics: ic u = 0 and u_t = div(flux) with a time-constant flux, so u(1) IS the discrete TRiSK divergence field and the t=1 error norms against d are pure spatial-discretization error (the linear-in-time integration is exact to solver tolerance). The keyed-factor wiring (bare-name observed aliases of the mesh subsystem's const arrays) follows problems/divergence_mpas.esm.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:mpas",
      "equation:divergence",
      "convergence",
      "unstructured"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Ringler, T., Thuburn, J., Klemp, J. B., & Skamarock, W. C. (2010). A unified approach to energy conservation and potential vorticity dynamics for arbitrarily-structured C-grids. Journal of Computational Physics, 229(9), 3065-3090. Eq. (21); section 3.2 for the accuracy of the midpoint flux divergence."
      }
    ]
  },
